  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 212 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThere is amplified ridging across the central Plains late this week \ninto the weekend as a western US trough slowly shifts eastward. As \nthe surface high pushes to the east Thursday night into Friday the \npressure gradient across the region begins to tighten resulting\nin potentially breezy conditions Friday and Saturday. Clouds \ncover will also be on the increase Friday night into Saturday \nwith warm but cloudy conditions. High temperatures both days \nwill be in the 70s with Friday the warmer of the two days. \n\nBy Sunday, the ridge axis will shift eastward allowing \nsouthwesterly flow aloft to develop with a shortwave trough \nlifting northeastward and across the area on Monday. This storm \nsystem will also bring a cool front across the area. There is a \nlot of model variability on the timing of this front as well as \nthe temperatures. There is a much as a 15 degree variation in \nmodels based on the timing of the front. High temperatures may \nlinger into the 70s on Monday. There are low (15 to 30%) chance\nof rain. Rainfall amounts are expected to be light with less\nthan a tenth of an inch expected. By Tuesday, high temperatures\ndrop to the upper 50s to lower 60s.",
